  it("finds this player's own ship among the ships in view, whatever their order", () => {
    const ships = new Map([
      ["rival", { id: "rival", x: 1, y: 2, speed: 5 }],
      ["me", { id: "me", x: 3, y: 4, speed: 0 }],
    ]);
    expect(flowModelOf({ code: "", worldTick: 0, ships }, "me", TILE).own).toEqual({ x: 3, y: 4, speed: 0 });
    expect(flowModelOf({ code: "", worldTick: 0, ships }, "gone", TILE).own).toBeUndefined();
  });
});
# match-online: branch coverage

Every room-level and UI branch that `match-online` (with its two rounds of fixes) added or changed, one row each: where it is, the branch in one line, and the test that fails when the branch is deleted. Each `tested` row was checked by deleting the branch on a scratch copy of the tree and running its tests; the row names the tests that failed (the deletion id says what was deleted, for rerunning). None of those edits is committed.

Rows marked `removed` are branches this round took out: dead code, or code moved into a tested function. Rows marked `equivalent` are kept, and deleting them changes nothing any player or test can observe, for the reason given. No row is `unreachable` or `untested`.

285 rows: 265 `tested`, 15 `equivalent`, 5 `removed`.

| # | Area | File and function | Branch | Test that fails without it (or the reason) | Status | Deletion |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Lobby and late join | `MatchRoom.ts` `onJoin` | Refuses a join once the flow has left its lobby (the room's own check, for a join the listing still admitted) | `tests/integration/lobby.test.ts` › the lobby (§2) refuses a late arrival at admission, before the room seats it, and in the room itself while the listing still says open | tested | `join-lobby-only` |
| 2 | Lobby and late join | `admission.ts` `authorizePrivateEntry` | Refuses a join at admission when the listing says `started`, with the started message | `tests/integration/lobby.test.ts` › the lobby (§2) refuses a late arrival at admission, before the room seats it, and in the room itself while the listing still says open | tested | `admission-started` |
| 3 | Lobby and late join | `MatchRoom.ts` `applyFlowEvent` `phase-changed` | Marks the listing started when the ready countdown begins | `tests/integration/lobby.test.ts` › the lobby (§2) starts only at the host's request with two or more players, counts down, refuses late arrivals, then gives every ship the departure's protection<br>`tests/integration/lobby.test.ts` › the lobby (§2) refuses a late arrival at admission, before the room seats it, and in the room itself while the listing still says open | tested | `listing-started` |
| 4 | Lobby and late join | `MatchRoom.ts` `applyFlowEvent` `phase-changed` | Reopens the listing when the countdown falls back to the lobby | `tests/integration/lobby.test.ts` › the lobby (§2) goes back to the lobby when a player leaves the countdown with fewer than two, and admits again | tested | `listing-reopen` |
| 5 | Lobby and late join | `MatchRoom.ts` `onJoin` | Reports the join to the flow | `tests/integration/lobby.test.ts` › the lobby (§2) starts only at the host's request with two or more players, counts down, refuses late arrivals, then gives every ship the departure's protection<br>`tests/integration/lobby.test.ts` › the lobby (§2) refuses a late arrival at admission, before the room seats it, and in the room itself while the listing still says open<br>(and 2 more) | tested | `join-report` |
